{"type":"text","timestamp":1784864195796,"sessionID":"ses_06dcedabcffenFAhCXYlY0mNab","part":{"id":"prt_f92323241001ZyYQUSypT5RS67","messageID":"msg_f923209d9001cBDF6QJe6JMxTw","sessionID":"ses_06dcedabcffenFAhCXYlY0mNab","type":"text","text":"Based on the query results, I found the ratio of outpatient to inpatient followed up treatment among SLE diagnosed patients.\n\n**Results:**\n- Inpatient count (Admission = '+'): **110**\n- Outpatient count (Admission = '-'): **84**\n- Ratio (inpatient/outpatient): **1.3095** (or approximately **1.31**)\n\nThe ratio is calculated as 110/84 = 1.3095..., meaning there are about 1.31 inpatient follow-ups for every outpatient follow-up among SLE diagnosed patients.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:** 1.3095 (or 110/84 ≈ 1.31)\n\n**Evidence SQL:**\n```sql\nSELECT \n  CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN Admission = '+' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS REAL) / \n  NULLIF(SUM(CASE WHEN Admission = '-' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), 0) AS ratio_outpatient_to_inpatient,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN Admission = '+' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS inpatient_count,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN Admission = '-' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS outpatient_count\nFROM Patient \nWHERE Diagnosis = 'SLE'\n```","time":{"start":1784864191041,"end":1784864195793}}}
